<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Kuna GH-1645: C++ catch handlers (option ehcatch off|catch|all, default catch).

    Issue: a landing pad is entered only by the unwinder, so the flow walk never
    decoded it. A function with a try/catch printed as its normal path alone
    (`work(); return 0;`), with no note that a handler existed. On ARM32 the
    tables live in .ARM.exidx/.ARM.extab, which kuna did not read at all.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 program prep decodes every LSDA
    (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/entry/kuna_ehtable.rs`), reached through an
    .eh_frame FDE or an .ARM.exidx entry (`kuna_armexidx.rs`, which also gives
    the ARM function starts); P2 flow classification
    (`p2_lift/kuna_ehcatch.rs`) gives a guarded call an edge to its landing
    pad; P8 prefers the handler as the `if` body; P9 prints the `if` as
    try/catch.

    Fixtures: `decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/ehcatch_x86_64.so`,
    `ehcatch_arm.so` and `ehcatch_thumb_stripped.so`, three builds of
    `ehcatch.cc` (clang 22 -O2 -fPIC -fexceptions, ld.lld -shared; the recipe is
    in the source):

      int guarded(int v) { try { work(v); } catch (int e) { return e; } return 0; }
      int sorted(int v) {
        try { work(v); }
        catch (const Odd &e) { return e.code; }
        catch (...) { return -1; }
        return twice(v);
      }

    `Odd` has hidden visibility, so nothing names its type_info but the
    object's own name string. `twice` is static: in the stripped Thumb build
    only .ARM.exidx states where it starts.

    Pass 1 is `ehcatch off` (the bug): #1 the header counts the hidden handler,
    #2 no handler prints. Pass 2 is the default on x86-64: #3-#5 `guarded`
    prints its handler as try/catch and returns the caught value, #6-#7
    `sorted` names both clauses and dispatches on the selector. Pass 3 is the
    ARM build, read through .ARM.exidx/.ARM.extab, and pass 4 the stripped
    Thumb build: #8 in both the handler returns the caught value from inside
    the catch block, #9 every handler reads the exception object the unwinder
    hands it, #10 the static helper is a Thumb function .ARM.exidx alone
    names, #11 no handler fell back to the plain `if (__eh_catch(T))` form.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
